      "human_symbol": null,
      "system_comment": "14...e5 is the strongest continuation, holding the balance (+0.16, Stockfish:16): Black's pieces are actively placed, and [pv:e5 Rfd1 exd4 Nxd4 Nf6] may pressure the bishop on e4, though in return White's rooks could become more active on the open files deeper in the line\u2014the...exd4 capture in that sequence can later win a pawn in the middlegame....c5 is a comparable alternative that leads to a slight advantage for White after [pv:c5 Rac1 f5 Bd3 b6].",
