      "san_match": true,
      "human_comment": "",
      "human_symbol": null,
      "system_comment": "16...exd4 is the strongest move here, holding the balance (+0.16, Stockfish:16) by winning a pawn\u2014a material edge that can weigh in the middlegame. The main continuation [pv:exd4 Rxd4 Qe7 Bh7+ Kh8] keeps that extra pawn in hand. Re8 is a roughly comparable alternative that leads to a slight advantage for White [pv:Re8 h3 Qe7 g4 Nf6], where Black may target the bishop on e4 in the line, but capturing on d4 is the more accurate choice.",
