      "human_comment": "Better than 26. Ng6+ Qxg6 27. Bxg6 Rf6 and Black still has sufficient forces\nto organize a solid defense.",
      "human_symbol": null,
      "system_comment": "The most accurate move, Bg6, maintains White's advantage (+1.40, Stockfish:16), and after [pv:Bg6 Rf6 Bxh5 Bxh5 g4] White is set to hold a queen and a pawn for a rook and a bishop\u2014a material imbalance that keeps long-term pressure. Ng6+ was a comparable option that leads to a clear advantage for White as well, via [pv:Ng6+ Qxg6 Bxg6 Rf6 h5], where White immediately has a queen and pawn for rook and knight and the line may leave Black's pawn structure weakened.",
