      "san": "Qc5",
      "human_san": "Qc5",
      "san_match": true,
      "human_comment": "",
      "human_symbol": null,
      "system_comment": "30.Qc5 is the most accurate move, though it lets White's advantage shrink in the main line. (+5.69, Stockfish:16) [pv:Qc5 Bxe6 Bxe6 Rdd8 Qxe7] The runner-up 30.f3 would leave White with a decisive advantage, immediately targeting the bishop on g4 and taking control of the center, which generally keeps Black's pieces tied down, [pv:f3 Bxe6 Bxe6 Ng8 Qc5] but it is clearly weaker than the queen move White chose; White later won the game.",
